# Service tests (`src/services/<service_name>/`)

## Location

- All tests for a service live in **`src/services/<service_name>/__tests__/`** at the **top level of `__tests__`** (no `unit/`, `integration/`, or other subfolders for tests).

## Allowed test modules (exactly these two names)

Replace `<service_name>` with the **service package directory name** (same as the folder under `src/services/`, e.g. `logging`, `text_to_speech`, `configuration`).

| Role | Filename |
|------|------------|
| All unit tests | `test_<service_name>_service.py` |
| All integration tests | `test_<service_name>_service_integration.py` |

Examples:

- `src/services/logging/__tests__/test_logging_service.py`
- `src/services/logging/__tests__/test_logging_service_integration.py`
- `src/services/text_to_speech/__tests__/test_text_to_speech_service.py`
- `src/services/text_to_speech/__tests__/test_text_to_speech_service_integration.py`

## Not allowed for the service

- Any other **`test_*.py`** under that service’s `__tests__` tree (e.g. `test_*_routes.py`, split files per area).
- **`unit/`** or **`integration/`** (or any) subdirectories whose purpose is holding tests.

## Exceptions

- **`__init__.py`** in `__tests__` is allowed if the package needs it; it is not a test module.

## When editing or adding tests

- Prefer **markers** (`@pytest.mark.integration`, etc.) or **class grouping** inside the two files to separate unit vs integration concerns if tooling needs it—do not add more test files to satisfy that.
